  <div class="section-label">Executive Summary</div>
  <h2>What This Report Covers</h2>

  <div class="summary-box">
    <p>This report analyzes the planning framework, property impacts, engineering design standards, noise abatement policy, governance actions, and financial timeline for the SR-177 Weber County extension. It is intended to inform all property owners along the 5100 West corridor in West Haven and Hooper.</p>
    <p>The segment from 1800 North (West Point) to 4000 South (West Haven) is currently in the State Environmental Study (SES) phase.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} Local officials have indicated UDOT is studying an alignment along 5100 West; UDOT has not published a preferred alternative.{% cite "whc-warnke-minutes" %} The project remains unfunded for construction. Utah's Unified Transportation Plan places this segment in Phase 3 (2043–2050), though local officials are lobbying for earlier action.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-2023-2050" %}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="callout info">
    <p><strong>Start here if you own property near the corridor:</strong> Review the <a href="property-owner-guide.html">Property Owner Guide</a> first. No parcel-level right-of-way boundary has been officially published yet, so the most important immediate actions are to register for UDOT updates, document your property, and watch for Draft SES maps.</p>
  </div>

